                        "review": "Owned this game for ages and every once in a while, when I just want to shoot things in a proper representation of cyberspace, I go back.\n\nWhile the game has been in EA for essentially the entire duration I've been playing, that's more a testament to the Dev not feeling it is done yet.\nBlack Ice is upported and still getting updates, which tend to broaden the game itself.\nBut even now it already offers a full game experience.\n\nAnd that game is cyberspace as you'd imagine based on neuromancer and the fluorescent neon lights from the 1980s.\nCombined with a shooter/looter that's just fun and can be as serious or goofy as you yourself make it to be.\nAnd a soundtrack that matches the visual atmosphere.\n\nAll in all, a seriously good experience!",
